url: "https://osman209.github.io/odd-sieve-cell-system/"
abstract: >-
  Seven documents on the elementary sieve of the odd numbers, developed
  as a coordinate system of lines and cells. Papers I-IV build the
  construction and prove what it decides; Paper V derives the point at
  which it stops from inside the construction rather than quoting it,
  and measures how much of the difficulty the framework can localise
  before failing to cross it. Statements that are only measured are
  labelled as such and listed together, and withdrawn results are kept
  rather than deleted. No progress toward the twin-prime conjecture is
  claimed, and no new bound. Four verification scripts regenerate every
  number printed, each exiting non-zero when its claim fails.
keywords:
  - sieve methods
  - twin primes
  - almost primes
  - singular series
  - Buchstab function
  - parity obstruction
  - sifting limit
  - Richert weights
  - floor functions
  - quadratic staircase
  - elementary number theory
  - reproducible research
  - negative results
